I just got NetHack 2.3 from Grape.  I have noticed a large
number of things I dislike about it.  One or two may be
bugs.  Perhaps some of them are just misunderstandings.


1. NETHACK.EXE is BIG!  V2.2 was about 350K, while this is
   about 440K, making it unplayable without a HD.  I have
   a HD, but not all my friends do.

2. When I enter a darkened room, I notice strange '
   characters appearing and disappearing around the room.
   The / (cursor select) command seems to have no effect
   on these.

3. The lighting in a darkened room is not uniform.  I have
   seen light patterns like:    ...
                                .@
                                 ..  which are quite
   annoying.

4. I have had more hitpoints than my max, esp. after
   polymorphing back into a human (e.g.  HP 36/35).

5. On an IBM XT it appears slower than 2.2.

6. Your dog's polymorphing seems permanent, although yours
   isn't.  (Weren't the stooges surprised when they hit
   my dog polymorphed into a dragon:  Moe hits Nappie.
   Nappie hits Moe.  Moe is dead.)

7. The stooges are stupid!  (Attacking my pet dragon!)

8. The dog appears to have an infinite appetite.  (this
   was also true in 2.2)

9. The kitchen sinks appear to have no use.  / (cursor
   movement) misidentifies them as corridors.

10.Even when you polymorph to something that forces you
   to drop your weapon, you can still pick it up, but
   not wield it.

11.When you are invisible, you should know where you are.
   After all, you do see the walls, so you should be able
   to orient yourself.

12.The RUMOURS file got smaller.

If you have an explanation to any of the preceding mysteries,
please give it to me.


